From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=8B=AC=EC=83=81=EC=9B=90?= <dev.chamomile@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:08:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] version: binaries report <upstream>-wick.<N>

Why: wick's releases are upstream's version plus wick's own number
(v1.18.0-wick.1), but the binaries print CARGO_PKG_VERSION, so a wick
build says `Firecracker v1.18.0` and `GET /version` cannot tell it from
upstream or from another wick release on the same base.

What: the release label comes from wick-version (crates/version), which
reads patches/base and patches/version at build time and expands
`wick_version::version!()` to the literal `1.18.0-wick.1`, a valid semver
string with a pre-release part. It replaces env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION") in
firecracker (`--version`, `--help`, the start-up log line, `GET /version`
and `vmm_version` in `GET /`), the jailer, snapshot-editor, rebase-snap and
seccompiler-bin. Format and compatibility versions stay upstream's: the
snapshot format and `--snapshot-version`, the API specification's version,
and cpu-template-helper, whose version is written into CPU fingerprints
that `fingerprint compare` checks. The workspace lists crates/version as a
member. test_api_version compares Cargo.toml's version with the upstream
part of the API's.

Test: `cargo test -p wick-version` and
`cargo test -p firecracker --bin firecracker wick_version`;
`firecracker --version` prints `Firecracker v1.18.0-wick.1` and
`GET /version` returns `{"firecracker_version":"1.18.0-wick.1"}`, while
`firecracker --snapshot-version` still prints `v12.0.0`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
